course: dictionary
lesson: 12501
title: Depict: show it or describe it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To depict something means to show it, or to describe it so that people can picture it. A painter depicts a scene on canvas. A writer depicts a place in words.
explain: «The painting depicts a busy harbour full of boats.» You can see the boats in the picture, so depict means show. «The author depicts the forest as dark and frightening.» Here the words paint a picture in your mind, so depict means describe.
explain: Ask yourself: is someone showing it with a picture, statue or film, or describing it with words? Either way, depict fits. In everyday talk people say show or describe, but depict is the word you will meet in art and English lessons.
fact: Depict is a verb: depict, depicts, depicted, depicting.
fact: «Depict» means to show something in a picture, painting, statue or film.
fact: «Depict» also means to describe something in words so that readers can imagine it.
fact: Phrases you may meet are depicted in, depict as, and the scene depicts.
fact: In everyday talk, people usually say show or describe instead of depict.
exercise: «The old map depicts the coastline in great detail.» What does depict mean here? | To run away from | To count carefully | *To show in a picture or drawing | To hide completely
exercise: «The writer depicts the village as quiet and peaceful.» Which word could replace depicts without changing the meaning? | forgets | *describes | hides | breaks
exercise: «The statue depicted a brave knight holding a sword.» What was the statue showing? | Nothing at all | A sleeping dog | A market full of fruit | *A brave knight holding a sword
test: «In the film, the director depicts the city at night as lonely and cold.» How does the director show the city? | As bright and noisy | As a place with no night | As empty of all buildings | *As lonely and cold
test: Ruby says, «The painting depicts a storm.» What does she mean? | The painting is a storm | *The painting shows a storm | The painting hides a storm | The painting was sold in a storm
exam: «Her story depicts a small fox who learns to be brave.» Which word is closest in meaning to depicts? | ignores | hides | forgets | *describes
